# Git before deploy

Before deploying anything to the server (scp, ssh, rsync, pm2 restart, `/var/www/zonic-admin`, API rebuild):

1. Stage relevant project changes (never secrets: `.env`, keys, pem, hardcoded passwords).
2. Create a clear, detailed commit message (why + what).
3. `git push` to GitHub (`origin`).
4. Only then deploy to the server.

Do not deploy-only and leave git behind. If the working tree is clean, say so and deploy. If push fails, fix auth/remote before deploying.
